│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fast_heap_packing_with_swap_refinement                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current `balanced_packing` implementation is the dominant cost of the algorithm       │
│                          │ (speed_score = 0.00, algorithm time 0.56). Its inner loop iterates over torch tensor      │
│                          │ elements and performs tensor element assignment per item, which is extremely slow in      │
│                          │ Python. I replace it with a heap-based greedy (LPT with capacity constraints) operating   │
│                          │ on plain Python lists, which reduces pack selection from O(num_packs) scans per item to   │
│                          │ O(log num_packs).                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, greedy packing alone leaves it stuck at gpu balancedness 0.66. I add a      │
│                          │ cheap local-search refinement pass: after greedy assignment, repeatedly consider the      │
│                          │ heaviest and lightest packs and swap one item between them whenever the swap provably     │
│                          │ reduces the weight spread (0 < gain < weight difference). Swaps preserve the exact item   │
│                          │ count per pack, so the output contract is unchanged. This improves both GPU-level and     │
│                          │ expert-level balancedness at negligible extra cost. The returned tensors are identical in │
│                          │ shape/dtype to before, so the rest of the pipeline is untouched.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0140                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ z-ai/glm-5.3                                                                              │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ reasoning                │ {'effort': 'low'}                                                                         │
