│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ gpu_pack_local_search_refinement                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current GPU-level assignment relies purely on the greedy LPT-style                    │
│                          │ `balanced_packing`, which gives no post-hoc refinement (balancedness_score_gpu is only    │
│                          │ 0.66). The makespan of a bin-packing solution can typically be improved substantially     │
│                          │ with a cheap local search: after the greedy assignment, repeatedly identify the           │
│                          │ most-loaded and least-loaded GPU within each (layer, node) and swap the pair of experts   │
│                          │ between them that most reduces the load gap while preserving the fixed per-GPU slot count │
│                          │ (each GPU must keep exactly `phy_experts_per_gpu` experts, so swaps are the valid move).  │
│                          │ The search is bounded (a few iterations per row, each O(num_packs * slots²)) and operates │
│                          │ on Python lists, so it adds negligible runtime compared to the greedy pass while directly │
│                          │ minimizing the max-GPU-load objective that the balancedness score measures. The refined   │
│                          │ `pack_index`/`rank_in_pack` are then fed into the existing `phy2pphy` computation, so     │
│                          │ downstream logic is unchanged.                                                            │
