│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ proportional_replication_with_sorted_placement                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the greedy "replicate the currently-heaviest-per-replica expert" loop in          │
│                          │ `replicate_experts` with a proportional largest-remainder allocation of the redundant     │
│                          │ expert slots. This spreads replicas across experts according to their relative load       │
│                          │ (instead of stacking replicas on the single hottest expert repeatedly), which directly    │
│                          │ reduces the variance of per-replica loads and hence improves expert-level balancedness.   │
│                          │ Additionally, the physical replicas are emitted in descending per-replica-load order,     │
│                          │ which makes the subsequent LPT-style `balanced_packing` (Step 3 in the hierarchical       │
│                          │ rebalancer) pack the heaviest replicas first — improving GPU-level balancedness too. The  │
│                          │ loop count drops from `num_redundant` full-tensor argmax passes to a single top-k pass    │
│                          │ plus a small per-row Python loop, so it is also faster.                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
