│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ balanced_pair_packing                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the pure snake (serpentine) LPT heuristic in `balanced_packing` with a            │
│                          │ balanced-pair "greedy matching" variant, as recommended. Items are sorted descending,     │
│                          │ then the k-th heaviest item is matched with the k-th lightest item (pair id = min(pos,    │
│                          │ n-1-pos)). Pairs are then distributed to packs round-robin with alternating (snake)       │
│                          │ direction per pair block, and the rank within the pack records whether the item was the   │
│                          │ heavy or light member of its pair. This guarantees each pack receives one heavy and one   │
│                          │ light item per pair block (heavier improvement over the item-level snake, which can put   │
│                          │ two mid-heavy items in the same pack when groups_per_pack > 2), while keeping the         │
│                          │ construction fully tensorized and loop-free via `scatter_` on the sort indices. This      │
│                          │ targets improved GPU balancedness while preserving the vectorized speed of the current    │
│                          │ implementation.                                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0146                                                                                   │
