│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two programs: the current program is fast (fully vectorized snake        │
│                          │ packing) but achieves worse GPU/expert balancedness (0.66/0.25), while the inspiration    │
│                          │ program uses greedy LPT packing per-row with Python loops, achieving the same balance     │
│                          │ scores but much slower algorithm time (0.56). The new program keeps the greedy LPT        │
│                          │ heuristic (which preserves balance quality) but vectorizes it across all rows: items are  │
│                          │ sorted once, then assigned one-at-a-time in a single loop over items (not a nested Python │
│                          │ loop), with the argmin-over-packs selection done as a batched tensor operation over all   │
│                          │ layers simultaneously, using masking of full packs. This yields near-greedy balance with  │
│                          │ only n tensor ops instead of O(n*m*layers) Python-level operations. `replicate_experts`   │
│                          │ and the hierarchical logic remain unchanged (already vectorized).                         │
