│ patch_description        │ Restructure the packer into three vectorized stages: (1) LPT greedy packing approximated  │
│                          │ by a tensorized batched-heap sweep (repeat interleave of loads), (2) full vectorized      │
│                          │ multi-pair swap refinement that resolves the best swap between the heaviest and lightest  │
│                          │ packs across all layers simultaneously (replacing sequential single-swap rounds), and (3) │
│                          │ a cheap pairwise-match pass pairing the heaviest remaining item with the lightest pack    │
│                          │ item set. All stages remain loop-free over layers and reuse the validated scatter-based   │
│                          │ index construction from the snake packer, so the packing stays O(1) Python passes         │
│                          │ regardless of layer count while achieving better balance than pure snake ordering.        │
