│ patch_name               │ joint_replication_packing_refinement                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current pipeline decides replication counts (Step 2) before GPU packing (Step 3),     │
│                          │ with no feedback between them. Per the recommendation, add a single tensorized refinement │
│                          │ pass after Step 3: compute actual per-GPU loads, and when the hottest GPU exceeds the     │
│                          │ mean beyond a threshold, move one replica from the highest-contribution logical expert in │
│                          │ the hottest pack to the lowest-contribution expert in the coldest pack by mutating        │
│                          │ `mlogcnt`/`phy2mlog` before re-running the packing. This jointly optimizes replication    │
│                          │ and packing, improving GPU balancedness without the expensive Python-loop swaps (keeping  │
│                          │ algorithm time low). Since after mutating replication we must recompute ranks and         │
│                          │ packing, we do the refinement on `mlogcnt` then rebuild `phy2mlog`, `phyrank`, and        │
│                          │ re-pack — all with vectorized torch ops, no Python loops over items.                      │
